  "Number": 22,
  "Question": "If \\(3x^3-9x^2+kx-12\\) is divisible by \\(x-3,\\) then it is also divisible by:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3x^2-x+4\\)",
    "B": "\\(3x^2-4\\)",
    "C": "\\(3x^2+4\\)",
    "D": "\\(3x-4\\)",
    "E": "\\(3x+4\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Let \\(P(x)=3x^3-9x^2+kx-12\\). If \\(x-3\\) divides \\(P(x)\\), then \\(P(x)=(x-3)Q(x)\\) for some polynomial \\(Q\\). Substituting \\(x=3\\) therefore gives \\(P(3)=0\\), which determines \\(k\\):\n\\[\n0=3(3)^3-9(3)^2+3k-12\n=3k-12.\n\\]\nHence \\(k=4\\). Now group the terms to reveal the known factor:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(x)&=3x^3-9x^2+4x-12\\\\\n&=3x^2(x-3)+4(x-3)\\\\\n&=(x-3)(3x^2+4).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThus the polynomial is also divisible by \\(\\boxed{3x^2+4}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
